                <pb facs="0814" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg800"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Field, Assistant Attorney-General, to United States
                        marshal, New Haven, Connecticut.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 1,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States
                        Marshal</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New Haven, Connecticut:</hi></p>
                <p>The schooners Fancy and Winona are at Milford, alleged to have violated the
                    neutrality laws. See district attorney, and take care of them and the men found
                    on board.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. A. FIELD.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
